  "salt": "YMlsfYho2qczbCytpMouyA==",
  "text": "Scáthach was one of the great warrior women of Irish legend. Her name meant shadowy one. She lived on the island that now bears the name of her school, the Isle of Skye off Scotland. There she trained young warriors into heroes. Only she knew the secrets that drew students such as the great hero Cúchulainn, who vowed to find her or die trying. A candidate had to cross the Bridge of the Cliff, a great chasm, to reach her school. Scáthach's curriculum taught feats with strange names: the apple-feat, the thunder-feat, the supine-feat, and the use of the magical weapon the Gáe Bulga. She also foretold her students' futures. In one tale Cúchulainn wrestled her for ownership of Skye, then left the island to her. Her gift to him, the Gáe Bulga, invited comparison to the sword Excalibur.",
